#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:2
msgid "API Authentication and Authorization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:4
msgid ""
"Snapd performs authentication and authorization checks before executing "
"operations that may affect system state or modify snap security policies. "
"These checks are applied to interactions with the snapd REST API, which is "
"the primary interface used by the snap command-line tool and other clients. "
"Authentication establishes the identity of the caller, while authorization "
"determines whether that identity is permitted to perform a given operation. "
"Many snap management operations - such as installing snaps, connecting "
"interfaces, or refreshing packages - may alter the system’s security "
"posture. Snapd therefore ensures that only authenticated and authorized "
"callers can perform such operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:6
msgid "User identities in snapd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:8
msgid "Snapd distinguishes between three related types of users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:0
#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:10
msgid "Snapd user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:12
msgid ""
"A snapd user is a local identity maintained by snapd. It represents an "
"authenticated user within snapd and is used when authorizing API requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:14
msgid "Each snapd user is uniquely identified by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:16
msgid "a snapd user ID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:17
msgid "a snapd macaroon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:19
msgid "Multiple snapd users may refer to the same store identity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:21
msgid "Store user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:23
msgid ""
"A store user is an identity managed by the Snap Store and authenticated "
"through login.ubuntu.com. Store users are uniquely identified by their email "
"address. When a user logs in using snap login, the store identity is "
"associated with a local snapd user. The Snap Store provides authentication "
"tokens (macaroons and discharges) that allow snapd to interact with the "
"store on behalf of that user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:25
msgid "Linux system user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:27
msgid ""
"A Linux system user is a standard user account on the host operating system. "
"System users are uniquely identified by their system username or user ID "
"(UID). Snapd may associate a Linux system user with a snapd user so that API "
"requests originating from that account can be authenticated and authorized. "
"In managed environments such as Ubuntu Core systems, Linux system users may "
"be created from system-user assertions signed by the device brand, or from "
"user information retrieved from the Snap Store for a given store user email "
"address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:29
msgid ""
"On system user removal, the Linux system user is removed as well as the "
"associated snapd user. The identity file ($HOME/.snap/auth.json) is removed "
"indirectly when the system user is removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:31
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:33
msgid ""
"Snapd authenticates users using peer credential passing, snapd local "
"macaroons, and Polkit authentication requests. Snaps are authenticated using "
"PID-based cgroup lookup to determine which snap a requesting process belongs "
"to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/api-authentication-and-authorization.md:35
msgid "Summary of identities and layered authentication mechanisms"
msgstr ""

